On Mon, 2026-09-07 at 14:33 +0300, Mantas Mikul=C4=97nas wrote:
> Hello,
>=20
> After upgrading an NFS server to kernel 7.2.2 (from 7.1.11), it is no lon=
ger
> possible to mount filesystems that should be handled by a "crossmnt" expo=
rt.
>=20
> For example, with /etc/exports being:
>=20
>  =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 /=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0*(rw,crossmnt,se=
c=3Dkrb5:krb5i:krb5p)
>=20
> and all clients using NFSv4.2, it used to be possible to either mount=20
> foo:/hdd2
> directly, or to descend into it through a "foo:/" mount.
>=20
> With kernel 7.2 this no longer works -- after mounting foo:/hdd2 all=20
> attempts
> to access it result in -ESTALE and the client's kernel complains about=
=20
> "fileid
> changed":
>=20
>  =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 # mount horizon:/hdd1 /mnt
>=20
>  =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 # ls -l /mnt
>  =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 ls: cannot open directory '/mnt': Stale file=
 handle
>=20
>  =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 # dmesg | tail -2
>  =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 [374226.359731] NFS: server horizon error: f=
ileid changed
>  =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 fsid 0:150: expected fileid 0x2, got 0x100
>=20
> Mounting "foo:/" on /mnt and trying to stat /mnt/hdd1 likewise returns=
=20
> -ESTALE.
> (Or hangs for a while if it's a autofs mount on the server side, but I=
=20
> switched
> from systemd.automount to regular non-autofs mounts for now.)
>=20
> In this case the server's root filesystem is Btrfs, additional disks are=
=20
> Ext4.
> Another system with the same problem has Btrfs for both the rootfs and=
=20
> for the
> secondary disks.
>=20
> Bisect points to commit 70b7e3526c53d9dd7caccdbeff5b0485640d8cf1 which=
=20
> adds a
> netlink interface for nfs-utils' rpc.mountd to use. Indeed if I disable=
=20
> netlink
> support there (adding "[mountd] no-netlink=3D1" to the server's /etc/nfs.=
conf)
> then crossmnt exports again start working as they should, even with=20
> kernel 7.2.
> I've also tried kernel 7.3-rc1 with the same results.
>=20
> Does this look like a kernel bug, or a nfs-utils (rpc.mountd) bug, or bot=
h?
> The server has nfs-utils 2.9.2.
>=20

It's an nfs-utils bug (I think), though I'm still confirming that. I
had Claude draft some patches, but they're still quite raw. If you're
interested in testing them, they're in my nl-crossmnt branch on github:

    https://github.com/jtlayton/nfs-utils/tree/nl-crossmnt

Thanks for the bug report!
--=20
